  "summary_en": "Binding AgID technical guidelines under Italy's Digital Administration Code on creating, registering, managing and preserving electronic documents. They cover protocol registration, classification, file formats, preservation systems, roles, security and GDPR compliance. They have no AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Guidelines are binding erga omnes and enforceable before administrative courts",
   "They replace the 2013 and 2014 DPCM technical rules on electronic documents and preservation",
   "Public administrations must appoint a document management officer and publish management and preservation manuals",
   "Preservation providers must meet ISO/IEC 27001, ISO 14721 OAIS and ETSI TS 101 533-1",
   "Security plans must follow GDPR Art. 32-34 and AgID minimum ICT security measures"
